# Project Instructions
- Use specification and guidelines as you build the app
- Write the complete code for every step. Do not get lazy
- Your goal is to completely finish whatever I ask for
- Do not attempt to install additional dependencies unless specified

# Project Overview
- GigaDB is a web platform for hosting and sharing scientific datasets, particularly in genomics and related fields. The platform facilitates data citation, discovery, and reuse in the scientific community.

# Tech Stack
- PHP version 7.4+
- Yii 1.1 Framework
- Frontend libraries: jquery 3, jquery-ui 1, bootstrap 3, font-awesome 4
- Composer for dependency management
- Docker and Docker Compose for containerized development and deployment
- Nginx as the web server
- PostgreSQL
- Testing tools: Codeception and PHPUnit for unit, functional, and acceptance tests
- GitLab CI/CD for continuous integration and deployment
- Vue.js for reactive frontend widgets (use only when explicitly specified)

# Project Structure
- `protected`
  - `models`
  - `controllers`: 
  - `views`: PHP templates
    - `layouts`: app layout
    - `shared`: reusable php partials
    - `site`: most public pages
    - `search`: search page and partials related to the search
    - `dataset`: dataset page and partials related to the dataset view
    - `admin*`: private pages belonging to the admin panel
  - `components`: reusable Yii 1.1 components
    - `controls`: resuable form inputs with built-in accessibility capabilities
  - `js`: reusable JS scripts
- `less`: UI styles, following SMACSS architecture
- `gigadb/app/client/web`: Vue 2.7 widget to upload large files with Uppy
- `playwright`: JS powered e2e tests
- `style-guide`: page to visualize a style guide for the GigaDB styles, separate from the GigaDB app
- `tests`: contains unit, functional and acceptance tests
- `ops`: Files related to devops
  - `deployment`: docker compose files
  - `pipelines`: modular configuration for CI/CD pipelines

# General Rules
- Adhere to standard PHP coding styles enforced by PHP CodeSniffer (PSR2 and PHPDoc rules)
- Adhere to Yii’s MVC architecture. Controllers, models, and views should be organized and follow the repository pattern
- Separation of Concerns: Maintain clear boundaries between different parts of the application
- Maintain a clear separation of concerns, avoiding business logic in views
- Use Docker and environment variables to manage deployment-specific configurations
- Rely on GitLab CI/CD pipeline settings for secure and environment-specific variable management

# Env Rules
- Sensitive credentials and environment variables are managed via .env and .secrets files

# Frontend
- Code for views is located under protected/views and protected/layouts directories

# Backend
- Code for models is located under protected/models directory
- Code for controllers is located under protected/controllers directory





